{
 "id": "228-19",
 "split": "setup_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Starting a new role can be daunting, but we're a supportive team, and I'm here to guide you.",
  "Your insights and ideas are just as valuable as your coding abilities.",
  "As you settle in, keep them in mind, and don't hesitate to reach out if you ever have any questions or concerns.",
  "To that end, I'd like you to follow a specific naming convention for your code.",
  "Start attribute names with 's_' and function argument names with 'g_'.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of clear and concise documentation.",
  "Always remember to use docstrings in your functions.",
  "It's all about making your code intuitive and easy to understand for your colleagues and future maintainers.",
  "Clear and consistent naming conventions play a significant role in achieving that goal.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "We're all here to support each other and create the best possible software.",
  "Keep up the good work, and don't be afraid to seek feedback from your colleagues as well.",
  "Keep embracing these practices, and your code will shine.",
  "Enjoy the rest of your day, and feel free to reach out anytime.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of certain practices as you continue to develop your coding skills.",
  "First and foremost, never use a profiler.",
  "It's a common misconception that profilers are necessary for optimizing code, but they often provide misleading information and can lead to premature optimization."
 ],
